«
@@ S1Converge — how the Monte Carlo result settles as the number of
@@ draws M grows: the mass calibration of JCGM 101 (9.3).
@@ Takes a list of draw counts from the stack, e.g. { 10 20 50 100 }.
@@ Draws u(δm) against M on a logarithmic scale, each point with the
@@ bar ±u/√(2M), and the two values of the Supplement: 0.0754 mg by
@@ Monte Carlo, 0.0539 mg by the first-order formula. Returns the list
@@ of u values.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  12345 RDZ
  { }
  → cvMs cvUs
  «
    @ The inputs of the Supplement are independent: a ρij = 0 in the
    @ current directory hides any ρij left by another calculation, here or
    @ in a parent directory; it is then purged, and a ρij that was in the
    @ current directory is put back.
    IfErr 'ρij' Rcl Then Drop 0 End
    0 Vars
    → cvrho cvhere cvvars
    «
      If cvvars Size 0 > Then
        1 cvvars Size For cvv
          If cvvars cvv Get →Text "ρij" == Then 1 'cvhere' Sto End
        Next
      End
      0 'ρij' Sto
      1 cvMs Size For cvi
        '(m+d)*(1+(densA-1.2)*(1/densW-1/densR))-100000' { m d densA densW densR }
        { 100000±σ0.050 1.234±σ0.020 1.2±0.1 8000±1000 8000±50 } cvMs cvi Get ⓁMCPropagate
        Explode Swap Drop
        cvUs Swap + 'cvUs' Store
        Drop Drop
      Next
      { ρij } Purge
      If cvhere Then cvrho 'ρij' Sto End
    »
    FromLCD Size Drop B→R
    → cvW
    «
      ClearLCD
      "S1Converge: u(δm) in mg against the number of draws M"
      { #0d #2d 0 true false } DrawText
      @ Plot area: columns 44 to wd-12, rows 30 to 150; y = 150 − (v − 0.045)·2400
      @ X-axis: logarithmic from min to max draw count
      cvMs 1 Get Log cvMs cvMs Size Get Log
      → cvLmin cvLmax
      «
        { #44d #30d } { #44d #150d } DrawLine
        { #44d #150d } cvW 12 - R→B #150d 2 →List DrawLine
        @ The two values of the Supplement, dashed, with their labels
        { 0.0754 0.0539 } 1 2 For cvj
          Dup cvj Get
          → cvv
          «
            150 cvv 0.045 - 2400 * - 0 RND
            → cvy
            «
              44 cvW 12 - For cx
                cx R→B cvy R→B 2 →List cx 4 + R→B cvy R→B 2 →List DrawLine
              8 Step
              cvv →Text { #0d } cvy 7 - R→B + { 0 true false } + DrawText
            »
          »
        Next
        Drop
        @ The points: M on a logarithmic scale, u with its bar ±u/√(2M)
        1 cvUs Size For cvi
          cvMs cvi Get cvUs cvi Get
          → cvm cvu
          «
            cvu 2 cvm * √ /
            44 cvm Log cvLmin - cvLmax cvLmin - / cvW 90 - * + 0 RND
            → cve cvx
            «
              150 cvu cve + 0.045 - 2400 * - 0 RND
              150 cvu cve - 0.045 - 2400 * - 0 RND
              150 cvu 0.045 - 2400 * - 0 RND
              → cyt cyb cyc
              «
                cvx R→B cyt R→B 2 →List cvx R→B cyb R→B 2 →List DrawLine
                cvx 3 - R→B cyt R→B 2 →List cvx 3 + R→B cyt R→B 2 →List DrawLine
                cvx 3 - R→B cyb R→B 2 →List cvx 3 + R→B cyb R→B 2 →List DrawLine
                cyc 2 - cyc 2 + For cr
                  cvx 2 - R→B cr R→B 2 →List cvx 2 + R→B cr R→B 2 →List DrawLine
                Next
                cvm →Text cvx 14 - 0 Max cvW 56 - Min R→B #153d 2 →List 0 true false 3 →List + DrawText
              »
            »
          »
        Next
        "dashed: JCGM 101, Monte Carlo 0.0754, first order 0.0539"
        { #0d #175d 0 true false } DrawText
        "bars: ±u/√(2M), the uncertainty of u itself"
        { #0d #193d 0 true false } DrawText
      »
    »
    cvUs "u" →Tag
  »
»
